s:
By Vieta's formulas, for the polynomial $x^3 - x - 2 = 0$,
\begin{align*}
a + b + c &= 0, \\
ab + ac + bc &= -1, \\
abc &= 2.
\end{align*}
Then consider the expression,
\begin{align*}
2a(b - c)^2 + 2b(c - a)^2 + 2c(a - b)^2 &= 2[a(b^2 - 2bc + c^2) + b(c^2 - 2ac + a^2) + c(a^2 - 2ab + b^2)] \\
&= 2[(ab^2 - 2abc + ac^2) + (bc^2 - 2abc + ba^2) + (ca^2 - 2abc + cb^2)] \\
&= 2[(ab^2 + ac^2 + bc^2 + ba^2 + ca^2 + cb^2) - 6abc] \\
&= 2[ab^2 + ac^2 + bc^2 + ba^2 + ca^2 + cb^2 - 12].
\end{align*}
From $a + b + c = 0,$ substituting $b + c = -a$, etc., we get:
\begin{align*}
a^2(b + c) + b^2(a + c) + c^2(a + b) &= -a^3 - b^3 - c^3, \\
2[a^2(b + c) + b^2(a + c) + c^2(a + b)] - 24 &= -2(a^3 + b^3 + c^3) - 24.
\end{align*}
Since $a^3 - a - 2 = 0,$ $a^3 = a + 2,$ and similarly for $b$ and $c.$ Therefore,
\begin{align*}
-2(a^3 + b^3 + c^3) - 24 &= -2[(a + 2) + (b + 2) + (c + 2)] - 24 \\
&= -2(a + b + c) - 12 - 24 \\
&= \boxed{-36}.
\end{align*}

p:
Let \[g(n) =
\begin{cases}
n^2 + 3 & \text{ if }n < 5,
\\ 2n + 1 & \text{ if }n \geq 5.
\end{cases}
\]Find $g(g(g(3)))$.
